# Shatter - Brother CNC Management Platform

## Project Overview
**Shatter** is a web-based platform for monitoring and managing multiple Brother CNC machines. Provides real-time status monitoring, historical data analysis, intelligent G-code file transfer, and NC program version control.

**Target Deployment:** Isolated local networks (manufacturing shop floors)
**Distribution:** Open source, Docker-based for easy deployment
**Multi-Machine:** Single Shatter instance can monitor and manage multiple CNC machines

---

## Architecture

### Three-Tier Architecture

```
┌─────────────────┐
│   Frontend      │  React/Vue SPA
│   (Port 3000)   │  - Real-time monitoring
└────────┬────────┘  - File manager
         │           - History viewer
         │
┌────────▼────────┐
│   Backend API   │  Node.js/Python FastAPI
│   (Port 8000)   │  - CNC communication
└────────┬────────┘  - G-code parsing
         │           - Business logic
         │
┌────────▼────────┐
│   PostgreSQL    │  Time-series + relational data
│   (Port 5432)   │  - Machine history
└─────────────────┘  - Program versions
                     - Alarm logs
```

### Containerization Strategy
- **Frontend Container:** Nginx serving built React/Vue app
- **Backend Container:** API service with CNC protocol libraries
- **Database Container:** PostgreSQL with TimescaleDB extension
- **Orchestration:** Docker Compose for single-command deployment

---

## Core Features

### 1. Real-Time Monitoring
**Data Sources:** HTTP endpoints (primary), FTP files (secondary)

**Multi-Machine Overview:**
- Grid/list view of all configured machines
- At-a-glance status indicators (color-coded: green/yellow/red)
- Quick stats per machine (current program, cycle time, status)
- Click to drill into individual machine details

**Individual Machine Display Panels:**
- Machine status (running/stopped/error/alarm)
- Current program name (from `/running_log`)
- Cycle progress (current cycle time vs. average)
- Workpiece counter (4 counters from `/work_counter`)
- Tool in spindle (from `/tool`)
- Current position X/Y/Z (from `POSNI1.NC` or parsed HTTP)
- Active alarms (from `/alarm_log`)
- Spindle speed, feed rate (if available)

**Polling Strategy:**
- HTTP endpoints: 2-5 second intervals per machine
- Concurrent polling of all configured machines
- WebSocket/SSE from backend to frontend for push updates
- Automatic reconnection handling
- Graceful degradation if machine offline

### 2. Historical Data & Analytics

**Production Logs:**
- Program run history (program name, start time, end time, duration)
- Cycle time trends and statistics
- Parts counter over time
- Machine utilization (operation time / power on time)
- **Cross-machine comparison:** Compare performance across multiple machines
- **Fleet-wide statistics:** Total parts, aggregate utilization, etc.

**Alarm History:**
- Alarm log with timestamps
- Alarm frequency analysis per machine
- Downtime tracking
- **Fleet alarm summary:** Most common alarms across all machines

**Data Storage:**
- PostgreSQL with TimescaleDB for time-series data
- Machine-scoped data (all records tagged with machine_id)
- Retention policies (configurable)
- Data aggregation for long-term trends
- Cross-machine queries and reporting

### 3. Smart File Transfer & G-Code Management

**File Browser:**
- Machine selector dropdown
- List NC programs on selected machine (via FTP)
- Upload/download G-code files
- Preview file contents
- Search/filter programs
- **Bulk operations:** Copy programs between machines

**G-Code Intelligence:**
- Parse uploaded G-code files
- Extract tool table (T numbers, names, descriptions)
- Compare with target machine's tool data (from `/tool` or `ATCTL.NC`)
- Highlight mismatches (missing tools, wrong sizes)
- Validate before transfer
- **Machine-specific validation:** Each machine may have different tool setups

**O-Number Management:**
- Programs uploaded with friendly names (e.g., "bracket_v2.nc")
- Automatically assigned O-numbers from pool (O2000-O3999)
- 2000 available O-numbers, rolling allocation
- When pool exhausted, recycle oldest unused O-number
- UI shows both friendly name and O-number
- FTP transfer uses O-number format (O2045.NC)
- O-number preserved across versions of same program

**Pre-Transfer Checks:**
- Tool availability verification (per machine)
- Work offset validation
- Subprogram dependency checking
- Warn on potential issues
- **Multi-machine deployment:** Upload same program to multiple machines with validation for each

### 4. NC Program Version Control

**Version Tracking:**
- Git-like version history for each NC program
- Store program content + metadata (upload date, user, notes)
- Diff view between versions
- Rollback capability
- **Machine deployment tracking:** Track which version is deployed on which machine

**Change Management:**
- Track what changed (compare file hashes)
- Annotate changes with notes
- Tag versions (e.g., "production", "tested", "development")
- **Deployment status:** See which machines are running current vs. outdated versions

**Database Schema:**
```
programs
  - id, name, current_version_id

program_versions
  - id, program_id, version_number, content_hash
  - uploaded_at, uploaded_by, notes
  - file_size, line_count
  - tool_list (JSONB)

program_diffs
  - id, from_version_id, to_version_id
  - diff_content, summary

machine_program_deployments
  - id, machine_id, program_id, version_id
  - deployed_at, deployed_by
  - status (active, archived)
```

### 5. Machine Configuration & Management

**Machine Registry:**
- Add/edit/remove machines from Shatter
- Machine profile (name, model, IP address, location)
- Connection settings (FTP credentials, HTTP polling interval)
- Enable/disable monitoring per machine

**Configuration UI:**
- Web-based machine setup (no manual .env editing)
- Test connection before saving
- Machine grouping/tagging (e.g., "Production Floor A", "R&D")

**Machine Health:**
- Connection status (online/offline)
- Last successful poll timestamp
- Error logs per machine
- Network latency monitoring

